{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523894-cult-of-ecstasy-and-euthanatos","id":1523894,"title":"Cult of Ecstasy and Euthanatos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-09T18:28:06-07:00","id":1523894,"title":"Cult of Ecstasy and Euthanatos","content":"It's a somewhat strange question, like I know that these two traditions had their disagreements in the past, in fact it seems like it was more than a disagreement, however I recently paid attention to the opinions or supposed opinions that are in each tradition's book, and from what I understand, seems that the two traditions have a positive thought about each other, in fact in the book of Euthanatos it is practically a love letter. Anyway, I wanted to know if anyone knows if there is anything that better establishes the relationship that one tradition has with another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T19:59:54-07:00","id":1523899,"title":"","content":"There's not a whole lot more, but I'm not sure what you're looking for. Both Traditions are made up of groups with long-standing relationships that predate the formal founding of the Traditions. Having common cultural backgrounds lets them have much better understanding, cooperation,and so on. Especially with both Traditions having their Indian-subcontinent factions being dominant forces internally, they have a lot of shared beliefs and paradigms that allows them to &quot;be on the same page&quot; philosophically in ways that doesn't translate as easily to the other Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T10:06:14-07:00","id":1523918,"title":"","content":"They're also in a similar position with regard to the other Traditions, having the whole benevolent, responsible core philosophies paired with practices that others look askance at thing going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T16:34:37-07:00","id":1523929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523894-cult-of-ecstasy-and-euthanatos?p=1523899#post1523899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not a whole lot more, but I'm not sure what you're looking for. Both Traditions are made up of groups with long-standing relationships that predate the formal founding of the Traditions. Having common cultural backgrounds lets them have much better understanding, cooperation,and so on. Especially with both Traditions having their Indian-subcontinent factions being dominant forces internally, they have a lot of shared beliefs and paradigms that allows them to &quot;be on the same page&quot; philosophically in ways that doesn't translate as easily to the other Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I just wanted to understand, for some reason I thought of them as opposites because one wants to enjoy life and the other has a purpose more related to death, but these relationships they have really give me the impression of a girl in love with a guy who has a mission in life that is slowly killing him, very cliche from a bad movie from the 2000s, I think. So I just thought: I'm probably romanticizing this thing a lot more than I should. So I asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T16:53:52-07:00","id":1523931,"title":"","content":"I does sound like you're romanticizing a bit. The two Traditions are opposites, but they're also complimentary. The Euthanatos aren't on a mission that's slowly killing them and the love from the Cult of Ecstasy is the only thing that will save them in the sort of cliche you mentioned. The Euthanatos are on a mission that puts an extremely heavy emotional toll on its members, and very few other mages understand what they're doing and why. The Cult of Ecstasy is their closest ally because they share a common philosophic starting point, and thus the Cult can be a source of emotional support that's not self-reinforcing like other Euthanatos can be, or misguided like other mages would be. <br /> <br /> The Cult is a therapist that has gotten the Euthanatos through some dark times, for a less romantic concept of their relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T17:37:10-07:00","id":1523935,"title":"","content":"Part of the Euthanatos philosophy is that for people to properly ride the wheel of life, death, and rebirth, they have to be free of pain, corruption, and other forms of psychic/spiritual trauma. So the Ecstatics and their philosophy of breaking free of various psychic/spiritual shackles, including those traumas, is somewhat complimentary to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T07:55:30-07:00","id":1524000,"title":"","content":"I recall that Malcolm Sheppard had a homebrew Mage setting that had the Euthanatos and Sahajiya as one group: they went out into the world learning how to live their best lives and teaching others to do the same, but if they came across any who dangerous and/or corrupting...out came the knives, so to speak. It was an interesting twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}